.TH RSYNBACKTUX\-BACKUP 8 "2026" "rSynBackTux" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
rsynbacktux\-backup \- run an rsync backup to a Synology NAS
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rsynbacktux\-backup
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rsynbacktux\-backup
copies the configured source directory to the rsync module of a Synology NAS.
It takes no arguments; every setting comes from
.I /etc/rsynbacktux/backup.conf
(see
.BR rsynbacktux.conf (5))
and is picked up on the next run, so no reinstallation is needed after a
configuration change.
.PP
The transfer is incremental. Patterns from
.I /etc/rsynbacktux/excludes.list
are excluded, and network mounts (NFS, CIFS, SSHFS, GlusterFS, Ceph) are
detected at run time and excluded as well, so a mounted share cannot end up
inside its own backup.
.PP
Only one run at a time is allowed. The lock is held on
.I /var/lock/rsynbacktux.lock
via
.BR flock (1);
a second run exits with status 0 without doing anything.
.PP
The detailed transcript goes to
.IR /var/log/backup\-to\-synology.log ,
rotated weekly with eight generations. Standard output only carries a one line
summary, which ends up in the systemd journal or, under cron, in a mail on
failure.
.SH SCHEDULE
Normally the run is started by
.BR systemd.timer (5):
.PP
.nf
.RS
systemctl list\-timers rsynbacktux.timer
systemctl start rsynbacktux.service
journalctl \-u rsynbacktux.service \-\-since today
.RE
.fi
.PP
The time is set by
.BR rsynbacktux\-setup (8)
in
.IR /etc/systemd/system/rsynbacktux.timer.d/override.conf .
On systems without systemd a cron job is used instead.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
All files transferred. rsync exit code 24 (files vanished during the run,
normal on a live system) is also reported as success.
.TP
.B 23
Not all files could be transferred. Treated as a warning when
.B TOLERATE_PARTIAL
is set to true.
.TP
.B other
rsync error; the original rsync exit code is passed through.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B RSYNBACKTUX_CONF
Alternative path to the configuration file.
.SH FILES
.I /etc/rsynbacktux/backup.conf
.br
.I /etc/rsynbacktux/excludes.list
.br
.I /root/.rsync_pass
.br
.I /var/log/backup\-to\-synology.log
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR rsynbacktux\-setup (8),
.BR rsynbacktux.conf (5),
.BR rsync (1)
.SH AUTHOR
https://github.com/W0rkingChr1s/rSynBackTux
